[
    {
        "content": "<p>Recently in FLT I have been getting a ton of warnings when compiling, e.g. </p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"bp\">⚠</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"mi\">3429</span><span class=\"bp\">/</span><span class=\"mi\">3481</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Built</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">FLT</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Mathlib</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Topology</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">MetricSpace</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Pseudo</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Matrix</span>\n<span class=\"n\">warning</span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">FLT</span><span class=\"bp\">/</span><span class=\"n\">Mathlib</span><span class=\"bp\">/</span><span class=\"n\">Topology</span><span class=\"bp\">/</span><span class=\"n\">MetricSpace</span><span class=\"bp\">/</span><span class=\"n\">Pseudo</span><span class=\"bp\">/</span><span class=\"n\">Matrix</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">lean</span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">'-/'</span><span class=\"o\">:</span>\n<span class=\"n\">Copyright</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">too</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">short!</span>\n\n\n<span class=\"n\">Note</span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">This</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">linter</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">can</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">be</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">disabled</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">with</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"ss\">`set_option</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">linter</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">style</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">header</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">false</span><span class=\"bp\">`</span>\n<span class=\"n\">warning</span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">FLT</span><span class=\"bp\">/</span><span class=\"n\">Mathlib</span><span class=\"bp\">/</span><span class=\"n\">Topology</span><span class=\"bp\">/</span><span class=\"n\">MetricSpace</span><span class=\"bp\">/</span><span class=\"n\">Pseudo</span><span class=\"bp\">/</span><span class=\"n\">Matrix</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">lean</span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"mi\">7</span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"mi\">0</span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">The</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">module</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">doc</span><span class=\"bp\">-</span><span class=\"n\">string</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">for</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">file</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">should</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">be</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">the</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">first</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">command</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">after</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">the</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">imports</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span>\n<span class=\"n\">Please</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">add</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">module</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">doc</span><span class=\"bp\">-</span><span class=\"n\">string</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">before</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">`</span><span class=\"kd\">@[</span><span class=\"n\">expose</span><span class=\"kd\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">public</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kn\">section</span><span class=\"bp\">`.</span>\n\n<span class=\"n\">Note</span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">This</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">linter</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">can</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">be</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">disabled</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">with</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"ss\">`set_option</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">linter</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">style</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">header</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">false</span><span class=\"bp\">`</span>\n<span class=\"n\">warning</span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">FLT</span><span class=\"bp\">/</span><span class=\"n\">Mathlib</span><span class=\"bp\">/</span><span class=\"n\">Topology</span><span class=\"bp\">/</span><span class=\"n\">MetricSpace</span><span class=\"bp\">/</span><span class=\"n\">Pseudo</span><span class=\"bp\">/</span><span class=\"n\">Matrix</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">lean</span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">'-/'</span><span class=\"o\">:</span>\n<span class=\"n\">Copyright</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">too</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">short!</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>No doubt this will be for some reason of the following sort: (a) in FLT we are currently sloppy about copyright headers and module docstrings (b) some linter has been turned on in mathlib (c) FLT copies mathlib linters.</p>\n<p>This is all fine, I know I need to write module docstrings for stuff which isn't being upstreamed, but for now I would like to turn the warnings off. I ran <code>lake exe runLinter --update FLT</code> but it didn't seem to fix the problem. Is there a one-liner which I can use to switch off the warnings for now? I think the key output in the warnings is <code>Note: This linter can be disabled with `set_option linter.style.header false` </code>. Is this something that <code>scripts/nolints.json</code> can deal with? Is this something which I can automatically make <code>scripts/nolints.json</code> deal with?</p>",
        "id": 592947606,
        "sender_full_name": "Kevin Buzzard",
        "timestamp": 1777972409
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>For hysterical raisins, <code>nolints.json</code> (and the <code>@[nolint]</code> attribute), and <code>set_option linter.... false</code> work completely differently. You should be able set the option <code>linter.style.header</code> to <code>false</code> in your lakefile:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"TOML\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"n\">name</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s2\">\"FLT\"</span>\n<span class=\"n\">defaultTargets</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">[</span><span class=\"s2\">\"FLT\"</span><span class=\"p\">]</span>\n<span class=\"n\">lintDriver</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s2\">\"batteries/runLinter\"</span>\n<span class=\"n\">testDriver</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s2\">\"FLTTest\"</span>\n\n<span class=\"k\">[leanOptions]</span>\n<span class=\"n\">pp</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"n\">unicode</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"n\">fun</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kc\">true</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"c1\"># pretty-prints `fun a ↦ b`</span>\n<span class=\"n\">autoImplicit</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kc\">false</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"c1\"># no \"assume a typo is a new variable\"</span>\n<span class=\"n\">relaxedAutoImplicit</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kc\">false</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"c1\"># no \"assume a typo is a new variable\"</span>\n<span class=\"n\">maxSynthPendingDepth</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">3</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"c1\"># same as mathlib, changes behaviour of typeclass inference</span>\n<span class=\"n\">weak</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"n\">linter</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"n\">flexible</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kc\">true</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"c1\"># no rigid tactic (e.g. `exact`) after a flexible tactic (e.g. `simp`)</span>\n<span class=\"c1\"># Enable all mathlib linters: automatically matches what mathlib uses.</span>\n<span class=\"n\">weak</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"n\">linter</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"n\">mathlibStandardSet</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kc\">true</span>\n<span class=\"c1\"># Switch off warnings generated by `sorry`</span>\n<span class=\"n\">warn</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"n\">sorry</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kc\">false</span>\n<span class=\"c1\"># Disable the copyright header linter.</span>\n<span class=\"n\">weak</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"n\">linter</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"n\">style</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"n\">header</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kc\">false</span>\n\n<span class=\"k\">[[require]]</span>\n<span class=\"n\">name</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s2\">\"mathlib\"</span>\n<span class=\"n\">git</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s2\">\"https://github.com/leanprover-community/mathlib4.git\"</span>\n\n<span class=\"k\">[[require]]</span>\n<span class=\"n\">name</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s2\">\"checkdecls\"</span>\n<span class=\"n\">git</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s2\">\"https://github.com/PatrickMassot/checkdecls.git\"</span>\n\n<span class=\"k\">[[lean_lib]]</span>\n<span class=\"n\">name</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s2\">\"FLT\"</span>\n<span class=\"n\">globs</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">[</span><span class=\"s2\">\"FLT\"</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s2\">\"FermatsLastTheorem\"</span><span class=\"p\">]</span>\n\n<span class=\"k\">[[lean_lib]]</span>\n<span class=\"n\">name</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s2\">\"FLTTest\"</span>\n<span class=\"n\">globs</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">[</span><span class=\"s2\">\"FLTTest.+\"</span><span class=\"p\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"c1\"># Build all files in the directory `FLTTest`.</span>\n</code></pre></div>",
        "id": 592955243,
        "sender_full_name": "Anne Baanen",
        "timestamp": 1777974482
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Thanks! I will end up with another technical debt tracker that way but this is fine. I think I'll make some technical debt issues to track these things.</p>",
        "id": 592956917,
        "sender_full_name": "Kevin Buzzard",
        "timestamp": 1777974976
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span class=\"user-mention silent\" data-user-id=\"238446\">Anne Baanen</span> <a href=\"#narrow/channel/416277-FLT/topic/warnings.20when.20compiling/near/592955243\">said</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>For hysterical raisins, <code>nolints.json</code> (and the <code>@[nolint]</code> attribute), and <code>set_option linter.... false</code> work completely differently.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>Is this to do with the difference between syntax and environment linters? Having never paid any attention to how linters work (this is not asking for an explanation, I know there are plenty about! I just know that if I read one today I will have forgotten its contents by next week) this is the limit of my understanding of linters.</p>",
        "id": 592957262,
        "sender_full_name": "Kevin Buzzard",
        "timestamp": 1777975086
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span class=\"user-mention silent\" data-user-id=\"110038\">Kevin Buzzard</span> <a href=\"#narrow/channel/416277-FLT/topic/warnings.20when.20compiling/near/592947606\">said</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>(b) some linter has been turned on in mathlib (c) FLT copies mathlib linters.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>If you are curious, what happened is slightly more interesting: it was actually enabled the entire time for FLT via the <code>mathlibStandardSet</code>, but the linter had been written in a way that it only ran for Mathlib!</p>",
        "id": 592962021,
        "sender_full_name": "Chris Henson",
        "timestamp": 1777976436
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Hah, thanks a lot for the explanation!</p>\n<p>The bottom line is that I am now being encouraged more strongly to put in copyright headers and module docstrings, which is definitely a good thing.</p>",
        "id": 592962897,
        "sender_full_name": "Kevin Buzzard",
        "timestamp": 1777976707
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Actually this linter is annoying in my projects since I don't want to be turning it on for files in <code>MyProject.Mathlib</code> which are short files whose fate is to be absorbed into an existing mathlib file (which already has a copyright header)</p>",
        "id": 592977852,
        "sender_full_name": "Yaël Dillies",
        "timestamp": 1777981219
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Would it be possible to switch the linter to taking a glob input, so that I don't have to disable it in my projects?</p>",
        "id": 592978079,
        "sender_full_name": "Yaël Dillies",
        "timestamp": 1777981284
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I'll de-lint my issue <a href=\"https://github.com/leanprover-community/mathlib4/pull/585\">#585</a> PR asap.  Thanks for organizing this!</p>",
